        'name': 'MORTARIA',
        'notes': 'Ex Tor. first sentence wanting in other texts. List. and G.-V. moretaria, from moretum. Dann. calls this “Kalte Schale” which as a rule is a drink or a cold refreshing soup, popular on the Continent in hot weather. Not a bad interpretation if instead of the broth the original called for wine or fruit juices. Mortaria are ingredients crushed in the mortar, ready to be used in several combinations, similar to the ground fine herbs, remoulade, in French cuisine that may be used for various purposes, principally for cold green sauces. Wanting in Tor.',
