            'step': 2,
            'text': 'Specifically: In a sauce pan put {{ing_01|oil}}, {{ing_02|broth}} and {{ing_03|wine}}, {{ing_04|finely cut shallots}}, {{ing_05|diced cooked pork shoulder}}. When this is cooked, crush {{ing_06|pepper}}, {{ing_07|cumin}}, {{ing_08|dry mint}}, {{ing_09|dill}}, moisten with {{ing_10|honey}}, {{ing_11|broth}}, {{ing_12|raisin wine}} (and) {{ing_13|a little vinegar}}, some of the gravy of the above morsels, add {{ing_14|red apples (or rose hips)}} the seeds of which have been taken out, let boil, when thoroughly cooked, skim, bind, sprinkle with {{ing_06|pepper}} and serve.',
