        'directions': list([
          'Crush barley, soaked the day before, well washed.',
          'Place on the fire to be cooked [in a double boiler].',
          'When hot add enough oil, a bunch of dill, dry onion, satury and colocasium [2] to be cooked together.',
          'Because for the better juice, add green coriander and a little salt; bring it to a boiling point.',
          'When done take out the bunch [of dill] and transfer the barley into another kettle to avoid sticking to the bottom and burning.',
          'Make it liquid [by addition of water, broth, milk].',
          'Strain into a pot, covering the tops of the colocasia.',
          'Next crush pepper, lovage, a little dry flea-bane, cumin and sylphium [3].',
          'Stir it well and add vinegar, reduced must and broth.',
          'Put it back into the pot, the remaining colocasia finish on a gentle fire [4].',
        ]),
