          'ROUX',
        ]),
        'name': 'CREAMED CHICKEN WITH PASTE',
        'notes': 'Spätzle, noodles, macaroni; this dish is the ancient “Chicken Tetrazzini.” Dann. Chicken pie or patty. tractum and gala, prepared with paste and milk. Cf. tractomelitus, from tractum and meli, paste and honey. Cf. Note 2 to ℞ Nos. 244 and 246. List. minimum; Tor. heminam; Sch. eminam. See Measures. The noodle paste should be cooked separately in the water. List. vel carptum, which is correct. Tor. vel careotam, out of place here. This sauce seems to be superfluous. Very likely it is a separate formula for a sauce of some kind. Seems superfluous, too. The noodle paste in the chicken gravy makes it sufficiently thick.',
