        'name': 'Fresh Ham',
        'notes': 'Musteus, fresh, young, new; vinum mustum, new wine, must. Properly perhaps, Petasonem ex mustaceis; cf. note 3. Hum. verum petaso coxa cum crure [shank] esse dicitur.... Plainly, we are dealing here with fresh, uncured ham. A certain biscuit or cake made of must, spices and pepper, perhaps baked on laurel leaves. Mustaceus was a kind of cake, the flour of which had been kneaded with must, cheese, anise, etc., the cake was baked upon laurel leaves.',
