        'name': 'Home-Made Sweets (Stuffed Dates)',
        'notes': 'Dulcia, sweetmeats, cakes; hence dulciarius, a pastry cook or confectioner. The fact that here attention is drawn to home-made sweet dishes may clear up the absence of regular baking and dessert formulæ in Apicius. The trade of the dulciarius was so highly developed at that time that the professional bakers and confectioners supplied the entire home market with their wares, making it convenient and unprofitable for the domestic cook to compete with their organized business, a condition which largely exists in our modern highly civilized centers of population today. Still being done today in the same manner.',
